    "narrative": "Today's slate presents a couple of marginal plays at best as we look to maximize efficiency for Ghost Ride the WHIP. At catcher, **Dalton Rushing** is projected for a 41.57 score against Robert Gasser. While the base projection of 48.03 was boosted by strong recency and Gasser's 4.14 xERA, the combination of a left-on-left matchup, Gasser's slow delivery potentially impacting **Dalton Rushing**'s stolen base threat, and his projected 9th spot in the order drag the score down to a marginal level. Similarly, **Brice Turang** is projected for 43.71 against Blake Snell. Despite a solid 4th spot in the order, Snell's elite 3.22 xERA significantly dampens **Brice Turang**'s potential.\n\nThe most interesting bench decision today involves **Tyler Soderstrom**. Though he is currently on the Injured List, his potential would have been a consideration if healthy. The optimizer's decision to bench **Brice Turang** (43.71) and **Dalton Rushing** (41.57) is a testament to the current scarcity of strong plays. With **Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood** all having team off-days, the depth of our bench is being tested. Both **Dalton Rushing** and **Brice Turang** are slotted to start only because of the lack of better options and should be monitored closely for any lineup changes or adverse matchup developments.",
